# Host deploy (this VM)

Cursor agent shells here run as the **catalog SSH user**. That user is **not** in the `docker` group and does **not** get unrestricted sudo. App code lives in catalog `remote_root`. Production units: **`portal.service`** (docker-compose) and **`elanflix.service`** (Streama JAR).

## One-time (root)

From a root-capable login (existing `ubuntu` session is fine for this once):

```sh
cd <catalog.remote_root>
sudo ./scripts/install-portal-sudo.sh <catalog.ssh_user>
```

That installs `/etc/sudoers.d/portal-deploy` (group `portal-deploy` only) and `/usr/local/sbin/portal-deploy` / `portal-migrate`. It does **not** add docker, a shell, or `ALL`. Re-login (or `sg portal-deploy`) so the group applies.

## Routine deploy (catalog SSH user, no password)

```sh
cd <catalog.remote_root>
./scripts/deploy-with-systemd.sh
```

That is `sudo -n /usr/local/sbin/portal-deploy` (restart `portal.service` + migrations).

- Portal only migrate: `./scripts/deploy-with-systemd.sh --migrate-only`
- Streama unit after a new JAR: `sudo -n systemctl restart elanflix.service`

Verify: `GET http://127.0.0.1:3000/agent/v1/jobs` → **401**.

Do **not** `su ubuntu`, do **not** use `DEPLOY_SUDO_PASSWORD`, and do **not** put passwords in git.
